WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:05.250
With an 85% audience score on Rotten Tomatoes,
you'd think "The Flash" would be killing it

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.380
at the box office.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:10.151
Unfortunately, this isn't the case, and we're
here to tell you why.

00:00:10.151 --> 00:00:14.260
After one of the most chaotic and controversial
production cycles seen in recent years, "The

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.570
Flash" is finally in theaters.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:17.860
"Oh my god!

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:18.860
Flash!"

00:00:20.127 --> 00:00:20.759
"Hi."

00:00:20.759 --> 00:00:21.730
"I love you!"

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:26.480
The superhero flick was released on June 16
in the United States, backed by a hefty budget

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:32.196
of $200 million, with an additional $100 million
reportedly being spent on marketing.

00:00:32.196 --> 00:00:36.740
As of now, according to recent box-office
reports by Deadline and Variety, it doesn't

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:40.801
look like Warner Bros. will be celebrating
the film's returns any time soon.

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:45.890
In the United States, "The Flash" only earned
around $55 million during its first three

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:49.177
days, and projections for the future are not
looking good.

00:00:49.177 --> 00:00:53.030
Internationally, the movie seems only to have
captured around $75 million.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:59.820
Overall, "The Flash" has only made about $139
million thus far — definitely not what studio

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.980
heads were hoping for.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:04.690
This may come as an awkward surprise since
the film was being touted as one of the best

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:09.570
superhero flicks ever made prior to its release,
with comparisons to "The Dark Knight" being

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.170
brought up earlier in the year.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.230
"Very poor choice of words."

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:16.560
Ahead of its release, the movie had several
high-profile supporters.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.700
Naturally, DCU boss James Gunn had monumental
praise for "The Flash."

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:26.422
Allegedly, Tom Cruise personally professed
how much he loved the film to director Andy Muschietti.

00:01:26.422 --> 00:01:27.872
So what went wrong?

00:01:27.872 --> 00:01:32.390
Simply put, "The Flash" was severely hindered
due to the nearly countless allegations against

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:33.317
Ezra Miller.

00:01:33.317 --> 00:01:38.070
With multiple arrests and accusations of assault,
allegations of grooming minors, and felony

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:42.960
burglary charges, the accounts against the
actor appeared endless before the film entered

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.390
its promotional phase.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:48.630
Asking even the most ardent comic book fan
to get thrilled about a long-awaited superhero

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:53.577
flick is a tall order when the main star is
constantly making headlines for all the wrong reasons.

00:01:53.577 --> 00:01:58.149
Of course, Warner Bros. worked hard to shield
the film from the immense controversy.

00:01:58.149 --> 00:02:02.259
Aside from attending the Los Angeles premiere,
Miller had next to no involvement in promoting

00:02:02.259 --> 00:02:03.000
"The Flash."

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.219
Sasha Calle, who portrayed Supergirl, was
a prominent interviewee leading up to the

00:02:07.219 --> 00:02:07.974
film's release.

00:02:07.974 --> 00:02:12.374
And, of course, the movie's trailers were
quick to put an emphasis on the multiple returning Batmen.

00:02:12.374 --> 00:02:16.840
"The Flash" featured Ben Affleck donning the
cowl once more and also saw Michael Keaton

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:21.214
reprise the role for the first time since
1992's "Batman Returns."

00:02:21.214 --> 00:02:23.440
"You wanna get nuts?

00:02:23.699 --> 00:02:25.825
Let's get nuts."

00:02:25.825 --> 00:02:30.560
Closer to the official release, smaller cameos
were also hyped; Muschietti revealed Nicolas

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.680
Cage would appear as Superman before the movie
was released, though he later claimed this

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.220
was an accidental leak.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:40.129
As fun as all these appearances and Easter
eggs might be for fans, Ezra Miller's name

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:42.479
is simply proving to be too cumbersome.

00:02:42.479 --> 00:02:46.569
Despite the glowing and well-publicized praise
"The Flash" received prior to hitting the

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:51.270
silver screen, the movie seems to be getting
a lukewarm response from critics, with a score

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.500
of 66% on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:58.680
The audience score was much more positive,
sitting at around 85%, and Cinemascore gave

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:04.572
the movie a B. In addition, Looper's own Dominic
Griffin assigned the movie a middling 5/10 rating.

00:03:04.572 --> 00:03:08.480
These certainly aren't the worst scores, especially
for a superhero movie.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.407
However, a film with the amount of baggage
"The Flash" carries needs to be great.

00:03:12.407 --> 00:03:16.180
It needs to inspire; it needs to drum up endless
excitement.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.955
In short, "The Flash" needed to be borderline
perfect.

00:03:18.955 --> 00:03:22.930
While an average Marvel film might have fared
okay with these reviews, "The Flash" most

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.980
certainly does not have that luxury.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.650
For about a decade now, superhero fans have
been wary of DC films.

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:32.680
While Warner Bros. has proven they can knock
it out of the park with some of their properties,

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:36.049
their latest films have received little fanfare
or worthwhile praise.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:41.110
"Black Adam" was released in October 2022,
and despite boasting Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:45.769
and a strong supporting cast, the film faltered
at the box office and received little praise

00:03:45.769 --> 00:03:46.769
from critics.

00:03:46.769 --> 00:03:47.894
"He didn't make it."

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:51.870
In March 2023, despite the success of its
predecessor, "Shazam!

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:58.239
Fury of the Gods" was met with dismal box-office
earnings, receiving only $133 million on a

00:03:58.239 --> 00:04:01.051
budget of around $125 million.

00:04:01.051 --> 00:04:02.581
Reviews weren't kind, either.

00:04:02.717 --> 00:04:07.500
Combined with Ezra Miller's numerous controversies
and the mediocre reviews, fans may have found

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.340
it easy to pass on the Scarlet Speedster's
adventure after remembering some of DC's latest

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:13.659
cinematic outings.

00:04:13.659 --> 00:04:18.220
Another reason that "The Flash" isn't performing
well is that "Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse"

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.909
was released on June 2nd, and its impressive
run at the box-office is still going strong.

00:04:22.909 --> 00:04:28.550
As of the making of this video, the film has
reportedly raked in close to $500 million.

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:33.220
And not too surprisingly, the Webhead is proving
to be tough competition for everyone at the

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.419
box office, not just "The Flash."

00:04:35.419 --> 00:04:40.560
Disney and Pixar's "Elemental" was also released
on June 16th, and is facing similar struggles

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:41.840
at the box office.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:47.780
With an estimated budget of $200 million,
the Pixar flick reportedly debuted at only

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.100
$29.5 million.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.840
It looks like "Elemental" and "The Flash"
might be on the same leaky boat, and that

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:56.070
rascal Miles Morales might be partly to blame.

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:59.819
It'll be interesting to track "The Flash"
as it treks through its days in theaters.

00:04:59.887 --> 00:05:04.316
It still has time to make some type of financial
splash, but it's not looking good so far.

